:"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Martin County has a record running from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle saw January to February at 19% and September to October at 42% of normal. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 35% on the middle. Grid 28643 shows a preliminary estimate of 149.3 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
